From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:53:46 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] viz: a software output device can offer a Direct3D 11 target
 (Windows 10 Mobile)

The seam for a compositor that draws most frames with Direct3D 11 where
ANGLE cannot run (feature level 9_3): the embedder's SoftwareOutputDevice
owns the device and the swap chain and offers them through
viz::W10mD3D11Target (GetW10mD3D11Target(), null by default), and
DisplayResourceProviderSoftware tells an observer when it lets go of a
resource's pixels, for a cache of textures made from them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
